# Output MAME and the tools write, never source.
#
# MAME creates a directory per thing it saves: snapshots (-snapshot_directory), controller and machine
# configuration (-cfg_directory), battery-backed RAM (-nvram_directory), save states (-state_directory), and
# some versions write .hi high-score files. tools/mame-diff/lib/mame.js already sends these under its own
# work directory, but a direct invocation (`mame coco -listslots`, a one-off probe) writes them next to
# wherever it was started unless it is told otherwise.
#
# These are unanchored so they also catch a run started inside a subdirectory. Nothing under these names is
# tracked, so no source file is hidden.
snap/
cfg/
nvram/
sta/
state/
*.hi

# Development tooling, not source.
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Local environment files (API keys and other secrets): never committed.
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Personal, machine-local instructions for coding agents: never committed.
CLAUDE.local.md
